@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Contract: Circuit Debugger
+
+## `simulate(gates, inputs)`
+
+- [ ] Returns values for all input wires unchanged → test: inputs echoed in output
+- [ ] AND gate: 1 only if both inputs 1 → test: truth table {00→0,01→0,10→0,11→1}
+- [ ] OR gate: 1 if at least one input 1 → test: truth table {00→0,01→1,10→1,11→1}
+- [ ] XOR gate: 1 if exactly one input 1 → test: truth table {00→0,01→1,10→1,11→0}
+- [ ] Chained gates fire in dependency order regardless of array order → test: shuffled gate order yields same result
+- [ ] Deep dependency chains resolve correctly → test: 4-bit adder computes X+Y for several values
+- [ ] Every wire (inputs, intermediates, outputs) appears in the result → test: result keys == all wires
+- [ ] Acyclic circuit given out of topological order still resolves → test: reversed gate list
+
+## `findSwappedWires(gates)`
+
+- [ ] Returns exactly 8 wire names → test: result.length === 8
+- [ ] Result is sorted ascending → test: equals result.slice().sort()
+- [ ] Correctly identifies the 8 swapped wires for a known 4-bit case → test: matches expected set
+- [ ] After applying the 4 swaps the circuit is a correct adder → test: simulate(repaired) computes X+Y on many vectors
+- [ ] Handles a large circuit (e.g. 45-bit, ~220 gates) under 5s → test: timed run with random swaps returns correct set
+- [ ] Works for randomized adders with random internal wire names → test: generate adder, apply 4 random valid swaps, recover them
+
+## Tooling
+
+- [ ] `npm run build` compiles clean
+- [ ] `npm run lint` passes
+- [ ] `npm test` all green
